From d24304ac14c930e57fd08f101a4b1427016c7381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] power: supply: add the SM5703 charger

sboot leaves VBUSCNTL reading 1800 mA, but the real input limit stays
near 500 mA until a host writes the register: the Galaxy Tab S2 charged
at +270-380 mA on a fast charger.  The driver applies stock's limits, a
TA 1750/2100 mA and a USB port 450/450 mA, a float of 4390 mV, and
stock's thermal rules on the battery thermistor, with one difference:
WARM ends at 43.0 C rather than 40.0, for with no cpuidle the battery
idles at 41-42 C and stock's exit would cap the charge at 83 % for good.

No interrupt: a 10 s poll, pulled forward by the MUIC's extcon events.
The MUIC reports a cable 30-50 ms before VBUS reaches the charger, so
while it reports one without VBUS the work looks every 200 ms.

The decisions are pure C in sm5703_charger_policy.h, tested on the host
by sm5703_charger_policy_test.c.  The gauge and the charger are built
in: the thermal rules must not wait for the root filesystem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
